abstract: >
  Reference implementation of the Isnād–Rijāl framework for claim-level
  provenance in multi-agent knowledge systems.  Adapts classical hadith-science
  methodology — graded narrator registries, weakest-link chain evaluation,
  independent corroboration, and dual chain+content criticism — to AI pipelines.
  Implements the architecture described in "Grading the Narrators" (Raja, 2026,
  arXiv:2607.24117).  Validated on 575,060 hadith chains graded against a rule-based
  chain-verdict convention derived from Ibn Hajar's 12 narrator tiers (Cohen's κ = 0.871
  3-way / 0.8667 5-way = conformance, not scholars' agreement; narrator-grade agreement
  0.331, context not a ceiling).  Measures error correlation across LLM transmitters
  (φ̄ = 0.5599, Kish n_eff = 1.626) and ships an opt-in lineage-aware Kish corroboration discount.
